# Unity C# conventions

- Prefer pure logic in `Assets/PaiSho/Runtime/Domain/` over growing MonoBehaviour managers.
- Managers stay singletons for now; do not introduce a second DI framework without an explicit task.
- Do not rename serialized fields casually — it breaks Inspector wiring in `SampleScene`.
- Avoid editing `.meta` / scene / prefab YAML unless required for the feature.
- Legacy `UnityEngine.Input` is used in gameplay UI; do not migrate input systems unless asked.
- Log with clear prefixes like `[BoardInteraction]`; keep player-facing strings in UI scripts.
